---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const findings = [
  {
    label: 'Where openness holds',
    title: 'Small systems can carry a long way',
    text: 'Open tools are most durable when people can understand and adapt what they use. Irrigation, crop-water modelling, forest monitoring, diagnostics, and logistics all show open approaches moving beyond experiment into sustained use.',
    links: [
      ['OpenSprinkler', 'https://github.com/OpenSprinkler/OpenSprinkler-Firmware'],
      ['AquaCrop-OSPy', 'https://github.com/aquacropos/aquacrop'],
      ['Open Foris / SEPAL', 'https://github.com/openforis'],
      ['CoopCycle', 'https://github.com/coopcycle'],
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Where the pressure appears',
    title: 'The hard part is not always the code',
    text: 'As systems become more expensive and dependent on large industrial or biological infrastructures, openness becomes harder to sustain. Farm automation, greenhouse control, livestock fencing, elevators, and bulk logistics remain places where access to a tool does not necessarily mean control of the system around it.',
    links: [
      ['Landscape synthesis', 'https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/blob/main/research/2026-08-landscape-synthesis-v3.md'],
      ['Grain value-chain scan', 'https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/blob/main/research/2026-08-grain-value-chain-open-infrastructure-scan.md'],
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'What people are building',
    title: 'Capacity is already distributed',
    text: 'The landscape is not a story of one movement or one model. It is a collection of capacities: people adapting equipment, institutions building shared infrastructure, cooperatives changing platform rules, and researchers opening instruments and datasets.',
    links: [
      ['Farmer-maker and retrofit records', 'https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/tree/main/examples/records'],
      ['Landscape currents', 'https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/blob/main/research/2026-08-landscape-synthesis-v3.md#currents-v3'],
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title="What We Are Learning | Open-Source Agrifood" description="A human-readable introduction to the research behind Building the Open-Source Future of Canadian Agrifood.">
  <section class="research-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">The research behind the gathering</p>
    <h1>What becomes possible<br /><em>when intelligence is shared?</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">We have been looking across Canadian agrifood and beyond, following the tools and institutions that can make knowledge more useful and adaptable.</p>
    <p class="lede">This is not a catalogue of projects. It is a way into the questions that brought us to the event.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="opening shell">
    <div class="section-label">A view across the food system</div>
    <div class="opening-copy">
      <p>Open-source agrifood is not one thing. It appears in software, hardware, public data, scientific instruments, and shared rules. Sometimes it gives people more room to act. Sometimes it makes a system easier to inspect without changing who controls it. Sometimes it is not present at all—and that absence tells us something.</p>
      <p>Our landscape now includes <strong>79 verified records</strong> across production, water, livestock, post-harvest work, diagnostics, processing, logistics, markets, and agroforestry. Taken together, they show an emerging field with real achievements, serious limits, and room to grow.</p>
      <p>In this context, “open” is practical rather than absolute: it describes how much people can inspect, use, adapt, and share. The significance is what that access makes possible—more capacity to work with systems, more room to respond to local needs, and potentially more benefit beyond the original provider.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="findings shell">
    <div class="section-label">Three things are becoming clear</div>
    <div class="finding-list">
      {findings.map((finding, index) => (
        <article class={`finding finding-${index + 1}`}>
          <div class="finding-label">{finding.label}</div>
          <div class="finding-content">
            <h2>{finding.title}</h2>
            <p>{finding.text}</p>
            <div class="source-links" aria-label={`Sources for ${finding.title}`}>
              {finding.links.map(([label, href]) => <a href={href}>{label} <span>↗</span></a>)}
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quote shell">
    <div class="section-label">A question worth carrying</div>
    <blockquote>
      <p>“The open agrifood layer has achieved robust, peer-reviewed, and production-proven viability across decentralized small-scale interventions, scientific simulation engines, and cooperative logistics, but hits a hard capital and biological enclosure wall at broad-acre industrial control.”</p>
      <cite>— Open-source agrifood landscape synthesis, v3</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="quote-follow">That boundary is where the interesting work begins. How might new intelligence increase the capacity of the people and institutions that feed us? Where could openness create real benefit—and what would it take to carry it further?</p>
  </section>

  <section class="research-cta shell">
    <div class="section-label">Keep exploring</div>
    <div>
      <h2>The full record is open to you.</h2>
      <p>Read the landscape synthesis, browse the records, and bring your own experience to the conversation. The event is an opportunity to put this knowledge in motion.</p>
      <div class="cta-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/blob/main/research/2026-08-landscape-synthesis-v3.md">Read the landscape synthesis <span>↗</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/metaviews/opensource-agrifood/tree/main/examples/records">Browse the research records <span>↗</span></a>
        <a href="/">Return to the event <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .shell { max-width: 86rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); padding-right: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); }
  .research-hero { padding-top: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 10rem); padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem); }
  .eyebrow, .section-label { color: var(--ochre); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; line-height: 1.3; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1, h2, p { margin-top: 0; }
  h1, h2 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; }
  h1 { max-width: 60rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem; font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 8vw, 8rem); letter-spacing: -0.07em; line-height: 0.92; }
  h1 em { color: var(--moss); font-style: normal; }
  .lede { max-width: 42rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.4; }
  .opening, .findings, .quote, .research-cta { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 7rem; }
  .opening, .research-cta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
  .opening-copy { max-width: 50rem; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .opening-copy p:first-child { color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 2.8vw, 2.35rem); line-height: 1.15; }
  .finding-list { margin-left: 20%; }
  .finding { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; padding: 2.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .finding:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .finding-label { color: var(--ochre); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .finding-content { max-width: 50rem; }
  .finding h2 { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; color: var(--moss-dark); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
